module v2.test.claim.local_binding_shadow_peer

import v2.std.integer { Int }
import v2.std.logic { Bool }

// THE SHADOWING SYMBOL, AUTHORED HERE RATHER THAN BORROWED. The defect reproduces on any
// module-level free function whose name a local binding reuses, and the first fixtures for it
// borrowed live corpus symbols (std.layout render, gunbc.plans.md_helpers p). Borrowing makes the
// fixture hostage to an unrelated module's shape: rename or delete that symbol and the probe goes
// green while the defect is untouched, which is the decoration DESIGN 4b warns is worse than
// absent. This one is owned by the fixture.
//
// IT RETURNS A CONSTANT true, WHICH IS THE POINT. Same arity as the local it displaces, and a
// Bool rather than a foreign type, so displacing the local produces a PLAUSIBLE ANSWER and no
// diagnostic -- the silent face. A shadow of a different arity refuses loudly instead, and that
// face is recorded in the witness annotation because a throw cannot be a witness verdict.
fn shadow_pred(n: Int) -> Bool {
  true
}

// THE SENTINEL PAIR, and it is a SEPARATE symbol from shadow_pred above rather than a rewrite of
// it. A Bool has two inhabitants, so a Bool-valued displacement can only ever say WHICH of two
// answers came back; an Int sentinel says WHICH FUNCTION ANSWERED. This one returns 900 for every
// input and ignores its argument, so it is total, same-arity, and same param-and-result types as
// the local that displaces it -- every axis held equal except the value returned. A witness
// asserting 2 and receiving 900 has located the producer, not merely disagreed with it.
fn shadow_sentinel(n: Int) -> Int {
  900
}

// NOT SHADOWED BY ANYTHING, and named so nothing is tempted to. It exists for the arm that asserts
// the module free function is still reachable when NO local binding competes for its spelling --
// the direction a repair that simply stopped consulting the free-function table would break.
fn unshadowed_sentinel(n: Int) -> Int {
  700
}
